# Testing (full: docs/architecture/testing-strategy.md)

- Table-driven, named cases, `t.Parallel()` when no shared state. Name tests by behaviour: `TestEnqueue_DuplicateKeyReplays`.
- Unit: domain, sign (golden + fuzz), config, SSRF policy, backoff table, handlers via `httptest` with hand-written fakes of consumer interfaces. No mocking frameworks.
- Integration: build tag `//go:build integration`; real Postgres/Redis via testcontainers-go (ADR 0005); real migrations; isolated DB per test/package; run with `go test -race -tags=integration ./...`.
- Subscribers in tests are `httptest.Server`, never the Compose mock.
- No `time.Sleep` for sync - injected clock, channels, or poll-with-deadline helper.
- Assert `errors.Is`, HTTP status, and envelope `code` - not message strings.
- Mandatory hard edges: backoff table, signature goldens, SSRF allow/deny (IPv6 + mapped), concurrent idempotent enqueue, lease expiry reclaim, crash safety, DLQ replay keeps history, auth matrix, secrets never re-exposed.
- CI: lint → `go test -race ./...` → `go test -race -tags=integration ./...` → build → image → compose config.
